WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.138
Unit 1 reads the guide's Step
7, which asks for five things.

2
00:00:04.138 --> 00:00:10.175
Run the drift classes: that's the run
command, with classes L D one to L D six.

3
00:00:10.175 --> 00:00:14.760
Fix at the source, not in the directory:
the period counts findings opened

4
00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:19.650
and closed, and keeps each unauthorized-write
finding's closure at the source.

5
00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:21.197
Report the six metrics:

6
00:00:21.197 --> 00:00:25.512
the run computes them and flags
any out of bounds or not measured.

7
00:00:25.512 --> 00:00:30.662
Prove the sole source for each
population: this code doesn't decide that;

8
00:00:30.662 --> 00:00:36.424
it's seven days of provisioning logs against
the audit log, in Book 03's Appendix C.

9
00:00:36.424 --> 00:00:39.453
And keep the evidence
outside the directory:

10
00:00:39.453 --> 00:00:42.563
that's the package, verify
and period commands.

11
00:00:42.563 --> 00:00:45.575
Book 03's Chapter 11 has the design.

12
00:00:45.575 --> 00:00:47.924
Attribute drift isn't this module's;

13
00:00:47.924 --> 00:00:52.030
it belongs to Gate 9 of the
attribute-driven migration guide.
